#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:42
msgid "A `BallFloat` is a closed interval $[\\underline{x}, \\overline{x}]$ whose two endpoints are `BinFloat` values. The examples on this page print an interval with this helper: it writes the lower endpoint rounded down and the upper endpoint rounded up, so the printed decimal interval still contains the stored one."
